1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:02:04,380
Please contact turkision@gmail.com
for any inquiries

2
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:07,970
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE FILMING
OF THIS PRODUCTION

3
00:02:11,281 --> 00:02:14,221
He who dies ends up under the dark soil…

4
00:02:15,196 --> 00:02:17,536
…and I am ready to take this sacred
burden.

5
00:02:19,086 --> 00:02:20,686
Allahu Akbar!

6
00:04:12,012 --> 00:04:12,832
You.

7
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:18,240
What kind of a devil are you?

8
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,674
Just like you they have nine lives.

9
00:04:23,124 --> 00:04:24,404
Osman Bey.

10
00:04:30,641 --> 00:04:31,761
My Allah…

11
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:37,263
…from the mischief of my enemies...

12
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:41,233
...I take refuge behind your greatness.

13
00:04:50,507 --> 00:04:51,437
My Bey!

14
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,080
With the name of Allah!

15
00:05:16,542 --> 00:05:17,932
What are you waiting for?

16
00:05:18,072 --> 00:05:19,052
Catch him!

17
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:28,280
Inform the soldiers immediately and
order them to blockade the forest.

18
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:31,250
They shall take the corpses of Balgay
and Cerkutay to Geyhatu.

19
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:32,690
Let them say...

20
00:05:33,990 --> 00:05:36,660
...Princess Sofia took care of Osman.

21
00:05:46,275 --> 00:05:47,385
Boran.

22
00:05:48,314 --> 00:05:49,314
Let's split!

23
00:05:49,314 --> 00:05:50,234
As you wish my Bey.

24
00:05:50,234 --> 00:05:51,164
I will find you.

25
00:05:51,164 --> 00:05:51,904
Go now.

26
00:06:39,966 --> 00:06:42,206
Do you want to be my daughter, Aygül?

27
00:06:44,837 --> 00:06:46,687
They arranged the wedding in a hurry!

28
00:06:47,427 --> 00:06:50,077
They made a vow of sheep and ram, of
horse and stud...

29
00:06:50,077 --> 00:06:51,717
...without thinking for a second!

30
00:06:51,717 --> 00:06:53,727
They created sorrow out of a fresh bride!

31
00:06:54,459 --> 00:06:55,229
Sorrow!

32
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:56,883
Sorrow!

33
00:06:58,827 --> 00:07:00,987
They created sorrow out of a fresh bride!

34
00:07:01,401 --> 00:07:02,401
Set me free!

35
00:07:03,104 --> 00:07:04,204
Set me free!

36
00:07:04,877 --> 00:07:05,787
Set me free!

37
00:07:07,568 --> 00:07:09,168
Set me free!

38
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:12,040
-Please stop, Aygul. Stop!
-Set me free!

39
00:07:12,894 --> 00:07:14,764
Set me free!

40
00:07:15,423 --> 00:07:16,893
-Please relax.
-Set me free!

41
00:07:17,267 --> 00:07:18,087
Set me free!

42
00:07:18,087 --> 00:07:19,067
Calm down!

43
00:07:19,798 --> 00:07:20,768
Set me free!

44
00:07:21,053 --> 00:07:21,953
Set me free!

45
00:07:21,953 --> 00:07:23,293
Aygül Hanım, please.

46
00:07:23,293 --> 00:07:25,013
-My Aygül, please stop.
-Set me free!

47
00:07:31,147 --> 00:07:32,197
Set me free!

48
00:07:38,256 --> 00:07:39,406
Aygül!

49
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:40,530
Aygül!

50
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:41,640
Aygül!

51
00:07:42,339 --> 00:07:44,379
Please stop and take a few bites.

52
00:07:44,379 --> 00:07:45,079
Aygül!

53
00:07:45,079 --> 00:07:45,939
I don't want to!

54
00:07:46,815 --> 00:07:47,845
Aygül!

55
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:50,037
Then you will rest for a while, huh?

56
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:51,610
They tied me!

57
00:07:52,010 --> 00:07:53,110
They tied me!

58
00:07:53,402 --> 00:07:55,282
They should tie her, not me!

59
00:07:56,312 --> 00:07:58,172
I brought you soup, Aygül.

60
00:07:58,782 --> 00:08:01,082
Please, you should eat something.

61
00:08:01,269 --> 00:08:02,569
I don’t want to!

62
00:08:02,757 --> 00:08:03,677
My Aygül.

63
00:08:03,677 --> 00:08:04,777
I don’t want to!

64
00:08:05,592 --> 00:08:07,532
Do you want to play a game together?

65
00:08:08,365 --> 00:08:11,135
Be my baby and I will feed you.

66
00:08:12,285 --> 00:08:13,045
Huh?

67
00:08:28,241 --> 00:08:29,041
Come on.

68
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:30,745
Take a seat.

69
00:08:42,172 --> 00:08:42,942
My dear rose.

70
00:08:48,256 --> 00:08:50,046
Let’s get our tummy full.

71
00:08:50,046 --> 00:08:51,026
My beautiful baby.

72
00:08:52,610 --> 00:08:54,180
Go on my beautiful baby.

73
00:08:57,713 --> 00:08:59,013
How wonderful!

74
00:09:05,035 --> 00:09:06,935
Go on my beautiful daughter.

75
00:09:12,055 --> 00:09:13,855
How magnificent my rose is!

76
00:09:13,855 --> 00:09:16,545
How magnificent, indeed!

77
00:10:24,875 --> 00:10:26,585
Just a little bit more patience.

78
00:10:26,585 --> 00:10:27,625
I am coming, my Bey.

79
00:10:27,625 --> 00:10:28,555
I am coming.

80
00:10:40,404 --> 00:10:41,354
Göktuğ!

81
00:10:42,957 --> 00:10:43,767
Göktuğ!

82
00:10:44,097 --> 00:10:44,967
Göktuğ!

83
00:10:45,449 --> 00:10:46,149
Göktuğ!

84
00:10:54,673 --> 00:10:55,453
Boran?

85
00:11:02,463 --> 00:11:03,833
Come here my brother.

86
00:11:12,391 --> 00:11:13,921
Where is Osman Bey?

87
00:11:14,827 --> 00:11:16,277
Where did they take him?

88
00:11:18,941 --> 00:11:20,701
Göktuğ, lie down my brother.

89
00:11:32,981 --> 00:11:33,991
Come on!

90
00:11:39,174 --> 00:11:40,234
Bamsı Bey!

91
00:11:53,886 --> 00:11:55,576
My Boran and Göktuğ.

92
00:11:55,576 --> 00:11:56,586
Are you okay?

93
00:11:56,586 --> 00:11:57,966
We are okay, my Bey.

94
00:11:58,506 --> 00:11:59,616
Where is my Osman?

95
00:11:59,859 --> 00:12:02,209
He is running away from
Sofia’s soldiers, my Bey.

96
00:12:02,209 --> 00:12:03,589
There are too many of them.

97
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:06,220
I don’t have another child to lose.

98
00:12:07,573 --> 00:12:09,623
Göktuğ, may you endure it, my child.

99
00:12:09,623 --> 00:12:10,403
Bamsı Bey.

100
00:12:10,598 --> 00:12:12,338
I can endure...

101
00:12:13,407 --> 00:12:14,727
...but my brother…

102
00:12:15,363 --> 00:12:16,683
…he is okay, right?

103
00:12:35,565 --> 00:12:37,825
Let’s see how thick your skins are.

104
00:13:42,281 --> 00:13:43,401
This way!

105
00:13:44,359 --> 00:13:45,319
Hurry up!

106
00:13:45,738 --> 00:13:46,758
Come to me!

107
00:13:48,882 --> 00:13:50,822
Come to me with your living deads.

108
00:13:52,116 --> 00:13:54,336
I will show you where I am headed.

109
00:14:07,651 --> 00:14:08,811
Go to this way!

110
00:14:08,811 --> 00:14:09,801
Block the path!

111
00:14:26,108 --> 00:14:27,088
My child.

112
00:14:28,171 --> 00:14:31,061
Allah knows the truth behind everything.

113
00:14:34,215 --> 00:14:38,215
Your brother is laying sick at the Tent’s
dispensary.

114
00:14:38,215 --> 00:14:40,265
He will get better with the help of Allah.

115
00:14:46,852 --> 00:14:48,742
What have I done to my brother?

116
00:14:50,858 --> 00:14:52,938
If something happens to my brother…

117
00:14:55,833 --> 00:14:57,433
...I can’t live, Bamsı Bey!

118
00:15:00,855 --> 00:15:02,235
What are you doing?

119
00:15:02,235 --> 00:15:03,765
What do you think you are doing?

120
00:15:03,765 --> 00:15:05,735
How would you explain this to Allah?

121
00:15:05,927 --> 00:15:07,107
Don’t you dare!

122
00:15:08,241 --> 00:15:10,801
From now on, being alive is illicit to
me, Bamsı Bey.

123
00:15:11,686 --> 00:15:14,496
My child if you take your own life now…

124
00:15:14,496 --> 00:15:16,836
…what is going to happen to your
brother’s will?

125
00:15:18,163 --> 00:15:22,743
I neither have lots of gold nor goods
and land.

126
00:15:23,647 --> 00:15:27,647
The only thing I can leave to you
is my loyalty to Osman Bey.

127
00:15:28,847 --> 00:15:32,357
May you be an Alp to Osman Bey.

128
00:15:32,933 --> 00:15:35,883
My blood and my life are yours, Osman Bey.

129
00:15:36,553 --> 00:15:40,553
You are free to ask for the head of that
Balgay dog.

130
00:15:40,553 --> 00:15:42,673
Just like you are free to take my head.

131
00:15:42,673 --> 00:15:44,243
The choice is yours.

132
00:15:44,243 --> 00:15:45,993
My life is a sacrifice on your path.

133
00:15:46,801 --> 00:15:50,441
What’s going to happen to those promises
you made to your brother and Osman?

134
00:15:50,497 --> 00:15:52,857
Do you want the Tyrant get away with
everything?

135
00:15:54,143 --> 00:15:59,013
Now, either stand up and fulfill your
promises…

136
00:15:59,013 --> 00:16:05,283
…or take your own life by contradicting
Allah’s words.

137
00:17:05,754 --> 00:17:07,984
Thanks to Allah, she attacked me, my Bey.

138
00:17:07,984 --> 00:17:10,154
What if she had chosen to hurt herself?

139
00:17:10,162 --> 00:17:12,432
Hopefully, this will be the last time.

140
00:17:14,115 --> 00:17:16,595
I just hope that your heart does not
become darkened…

141
00:17:16,595 --> 00:17:17,715
…and narrowed.

142
00:17:18,930 --> 00:17:20,620
Since I am located there…

143
00:17:21,994 --> 00:17:24,164
…when your heart gets darkened…

144
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:26,650
…so do I.

145
00:17:27,759 --> 00:17:29,039
This is the reason.

146
00:17:30,922 --> 00:17:32,102
Don’t be sad.

147
00:17:33,219 --> 00:17:35,159
I beg you, please don’t be sad.

148
00:17:35,852 --> 00:17:36,762
In this life…

149
00:17:38,272 --> 00:17:40,532
…my fortune got better only with your
presence.

150
00:17:40,848 --> 00:17:44,848
I did not know your value for
years, Hazal.

151
00:17:45,992 --> 00:17:51,372
Everything would have been different if we
were together since the beginning.

152
00:17:52,024 --> 00:17:54,224
You would have taken care after me.

153
00:17:54,307 --> 00:17:57,077
And I would not have turned out like this
in the end.

154
00:17:57,345 --> 00:17:59,685
Maybe it was Allah’s will to come
together now.

155
00:17:59,844 --> 00:18:00,914
The past is past.

156
00:18:02,353 --> 00:18:04,683
We are one and together from now on.

157
00:18:04,986 --> 00:18:09,976
I will always support you with
my prayers, love, and everything, my Bey.

158
00:18:12,063 --> 00:18:14,083
We will fight against everything together.

159
00:18:14,750 --> 00:18:16,760
Just like we will deal with everything.

160
00:18:17,286 --> 00:18:19,856
Yes, we will deal with everything
together, my Hazal.

161
00:18:19,856 --> 00:18:20,966
Together.

162
00:18:21,761 --> 00:18:23,281
May Allah never take us apart.

163
00:18:24,563 --> 00:18:25,673
Amin.

164
00:18:47,722 --> 00:18:48,912
What now?

165
00:18:49,463 --> 00:18:51,873
You have nowhere to run, Osman Bey.

166
00:18:54,981 --> 00:18:57,871
They killed my father in Constantinopolis
because of you.

167
00:19:00,470 --> 00:19:03,500
I made a promise to my father
before he died.

168
00:19:05,267 --> 00:19:08,207
Today, I am going to fulfil
his last wish.

169
00:19:08,426 --> 00:19:10,486
Such a dutiful child you are, Sofia.

170
00:19:15,247 --> 00:19:22,757
His last wish was to bury you under
the very lands you took away from us.

171
00:19:26,511 --> 00:19:32,151
This dutiful child is going to do
what she promised.

172
00:19:32,647 --> 00:19:34,147
You lost, Sofia!

173
00:19:35,679 --> 00:19:39,679
I spoiled both of your games!

174
00:19:41,845 --> 00:19:44,645
Both Subutay and Balgay could not
fight against us.

175
00:19:44,929 --> 00:19:47,059
Geyhatu is not going to be an exception.

176
00:19:48,446 --> 00:19:55,536
You will never take back the lands
my father conquered.

177
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:59,630
We never lose, Osman.

178
00:20:01,542 --> 00:20:04,782
Thanks to you, we formed an alliance
with Geyhatu.

179
00:20:05,328 --> 00:20:07,028
I got stronger because of this.

180
00:20:07,530 --> 00:20:10,790
I am going to create
a new order with Monks.

181
00:20:11,593 --> 00:20:13,843
Eventually, I will sit on
my rightful throne.

182
00:20:17,441 --> 00:20:21,931
You are dead, now.

183
00:20:25,396 --> 00:20:26,726
Catch him!

184
00:20:28,015 --> 00:20:29,865
With the name of Allah!

185
00:20:37,532 --> 00:20:40,812
I wish we found a cure for my Aygul.

186
00:20:40,987 --> 00:20:43,907
My own child is chained down.

187
00:20:44,874 --> 00:20:47,194
How can a father’s heart bare this pain?

188
00:20:48,878 --> 00:20:52,328
I have a cure in mind.

189
00:20:52,932 --> 00:20:55,862
However, I’m not sure if you will like it.

190
00:20:56,099 --> 00:20:59,839
Tell me, Hatun!
What is it? Tell me!

191
00:21:00,165 --> 00:21:02,935
If there is a cure I will
bring it from Baghdad.

192
00:21:03,298 --> 00:21:06,258
Our Aygul’s cure is not that far away.

193
00:21:06,569 --> 00:21:08,029
It’s very close.

194
00:21:08,029 --> 00:21:11,279
What are you talking about, Hatun?

195
00:21:11,935 --> 00:21:14,525
My Dündar...
My Bey...

196
00:21:14,747 --> 00:21:17,397
Let’s send our Aygul to Kastamonu.

197
00:21:17,644 --> 00:21:22,164
Near our Tent, in Seydihan,
there are famous physicians.

198
00:21:22,781 --> 00:21:26,211
Many people go there
to find cures for unknown diseases.

199
00:21:26,511 --> 00:21:29,641
The air and water
there are very different.

200
00:21:29,846 --> 00:21:33,566
Unlike this place which
is a burned down Tent.

201
00:21:33,566 --> 00:21:36,716
Wars, raids, martyrs.

202
00:21:38,527 --> 00:21:40,617
What do we have except Bala?

203
00:21:40,617 --> 00:21:42,687
And she can not be
sufficient for everyone.

204
00:21:44,209 --> 00:21:50,159
I don't think we'll find any cures
for our child here.

205
00:21:56,754 --> 00:22:00,754
Our Aygül needs fresh air, Bey.

206
00:22:01,306 --> 00:22:04,636
How can she find that air in this Tent?

207
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:09,790
She'll be very comfortable there.

208
00:22:10,230 --> 00:22:14,230
She'll be protected and looked after.

209
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:22,998
I don't know if you have
anything better in mind.

210
00:22:29,707 --> 00:22:34,667
you're right, Hatun.
Our troubles are enough for us.

211
00:22:35,271 --> 00:22:39,551
The girl will be wasted here,
you're right.

212
00:22:41,872 --> 00:22:45,492
A beautiful girl will go to waste.

213
00:22:48,051 --> 00:22:53,341
Okay. We shall send here immediately.
Even your words refreshed me.

214
00:22:53,474 --> 00:22:57,494
This will be good for my Aygül.

215
00:22:57,741 --> 00:22:59,141
With Allah's help.

216
00:24:12,267 --> 00:24:16,357
My Osman! Oh my!
Are you okay?

217
00:24:18,703 --> 00:24:20,823
What do you mean
Aygül attacked you, mother?

218
00:24:21,242 --> 00:24:24,542
She's crazy, son.
She's out of her mind.

219
00:24:24,596 --> 00:24:29,656
Anyway. I'll send her to the physicians
near my brother.

220
00:24:30,128 --> 00:24:32,858
Tell me what my brother said.

221
00:24:37,968 --> 00:24:41,138
Geyhatu comes like a flood
and burns like fire, he said.

222
00:24:42,133 --> 00:24:45,423
He doesn't want any trouble
in Söğüt or Kayı Tent.

223
00:24:46,255 --> 00:24:50,255
- Sensitive times, mother.
- We know that!

224
00:24:50,255 --> 00:24:53,635
What are his orders? Tell me that!

225
00:24:54,003 --> 00:25:01,203
He'll calm Geyhatu down so that he doesn't
slaughter all the Turks around here.

226
00:25:01,203 --> 00:25:03,023
He'll do everything necessary.

227
00:25:03,257 --> 00:25:04,117
But...

228
00:25:06,746 --> 00:25:09,796
He wants us to stop Osman from acting mad.

229
00:25:12,647 --> 00:25:16,477
Osman fell into Sofia's trap.

230
00:25:16,817 --> 00:25:18,327
He's done.

231
00:25:20,610 --> 00:25:23,230
The bad news will be here before sunset.

232
00:25:23,453 --> 00:25:27,453
Let's see. Because my aunt is watching
the Tent.

233
00:25:27,838 --> 00:25:31,388
He doesn't want any Muslim blood to spill
because of a mad young man.

234
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:34,640
He wants to know everything.

235
00:25:34,640 --> 00:25:40,800
He emphasised. Hazal Hatun
should prepare Dündar, he said.

236
00:25:45,026 --> 00:25:50,776
This is now our time.

237
00:26:00,281 --> 00:26:02,951
Sofia!
Protect the Princess!

238
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:32,400
Come on, my valiant!

239
00:26:56,793 --> 00:27:00,073
Don't let them get away!
To the horses!

240
00:27:00,993 --> 00:27:01,983
Quick!

241
00:27:05,024 --> 00:27:06,044
Quick!

242
00:27:53,367 --> 00:27:58,387
My Aygül...
My gracious daughter.

243
00:27:59,426 --> 00:28:02,206
I realised what I've done to you
too late.

244
00:28:02,749 --> 00:28:09,139
My insides hurt every time I see you.
I can't stand it.

245
00:28:09,719 --> 00:28:17,450
But I found a solution. There are famous
physicians in Kastamonu Seyidiyan.

246
00:28:18,552 --> 00:28:24,972
You'll go there and come back
as my Aygül, with Allah's help.

247
00:28:28,804 --> 00:28:30,644
These lands are harsh, my daughter.

248
00:28:31,961 --> 00:28:38,331
Let alone breathing, even staying
alive is a matter of luck.

249
00:28:42,569 --> 00:28:47,449
What do you say, daughter?
Do you want to go?

250
00:28:48,818 --> 00:28:51,088
This is the best way.

251
00:28:52,518 --> 00:28:58,888
I'll harden my heart
and you'll return to the Tent recovered.

252
00:29:33,338 --> 00:29:36,078
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim

253
00:29:41,358 --> 00:29:43,728
You called me, Hazal Hatun.

254
00:29:44,617 --> 00:29:46,437
Are you hungry, my lion?

255
00:29:46,674 --> 00:29:50,674
Excuse me, Hazal Hatun.
How could I dine on your table?

256
00:29:53,476 --> 00:29:57,476
We thought you were our son.
Have a seat.

257
00:30:04,234 --> 00:30:06,084
Do as I say.

258
00:30:16,878 --> 00:30:20,528
You asked to be an Alp and
I sent you to practice.

259
00:30:22,670 --> 00:30:27,670
You asked for friendship and
I put you on Dündar's side.

260
00:30:29,336 --> 00:30:31,576
I'm basically a mother to you, son.

261
00:30:34,014 --> 00:30:38,014
Now I expect you to return
the favour as a child.

262
00:30:39,344 --> 00:30:41,254
I'll do as you order, Hazal Hatun.

263
00:30:43,126 --> 00:30:45,746
I don't like to beat around the bush.

264
00:30:46,386 --> 00:30:49,396
You know what Aygül has done to me.

265
00:30:50,380 --> 00:30:53,950
I've heard. I'm sorry.

266
00:30:54,489 --> 00:31:02,589
Thank you. You also know what happens
to those who try to take my life.

267
00:31:06,474 --> 00:31:11,904
Aygül will be setting off.
And you'll go with her.

268
00:31:12,556 --> 00:31:15,466
You'll do what's necessary...

269
00:31:15,965 --> 00:31:18,825
Vultures will get her dead body.

270
00:31:20,525 --> 00:31:23,195
If he hears about it,
Dündar Bey will end my bloodline.

271
00:31:24,158 --> 00:31:27,408
She's out of her mind, Hazal Hatun.

272
00:31:40,753 --> 00:31:42,943
That what I'm saying.

273
00:31:44,283 --> 00:31:45,883
She's out of her mind.

274
00:31:47,987 --> 00:31:51,987
If she was to fell from somewhere,
Allah forbid...

275
00:31:52,184 --> 00:31:57,674
If she was to throw herself from a cliff,
who could hold you responsible?

276
00:32:04,619 --> 00:32:10,349
If he finds out that you killed Aygül...

277
00:32:12,335 --> 00:32:16,085
... Dündar will kill you.

278
00:32:19,094 --> 00:32:22,854
If you can't kill Aygül...

279
00:32:23,159 --> 00:32:26,489
... I will make you beg for death.

280
00:32:30,280 --> 00:32:34,480
I called you my lion.
Act like one!

281
00:32:37,324 --> 00:32:39,884
No need to be a hare.

282
00:32:44,098 --> 00:32:46,118
As you order, Hazal Hatun.

283
00:33:27,656 --> 00:33:28,966
They're gone.

284
00:33:30,784 --> 00:33:35,034
- We'll keep searching.
- Osman is a master predator.

285
00:33:35,878 --> 00:33:38,578
Finding him in a forest
is almost impossible.

286
00:33:38,698 --> 00:33:42,838
He's badly hurt.
We can't get such an opportunity again.

287
00:33:42,838 --> 00:33:45,448
We won't find him if we give up now.

288
00:33:47,015 --> 00:33:50,835
Kayı's borders are from this
point forward. We might fall into a trap.

289
00:33:52,869 --> 00:33:56,199
I was never this close to killing him.

290
00:33:57,716 --> 00:34:03,836
You're right. But the state
of our soldiers isn't good.

291
00:34:04,490 --> 00:34:07,050
Don't be stubborn.
We should go back to the castle.

292
00:34:21,901 --> 00:34:25,021
This is just the beginning, Osman.

293
00:34:25,376 --> 00:34:27,936
These lands will be your grave.

294
00:34:30,207 --> 00:34:34,207
We're going back to the castle.

295
00:34:34,782 --> 00:34:35,912
Let's go.

296
00:34:41,007 --> 00:34:45,007
Oh, Osman!

297
00:34:45,661 --> 00:34:50,381
Oh, my valiant.
Son...

298
00:34:50,779 --> 00:34:55,259
We need to sear your wound. But
we can't light fires, Sofia is after us.

299
00:34:55,496 --> 00:34:58,636
We need to go to the Tent
as soon as possible.

300
00:35:22,629 --> 00:35:24,389
What's up with him?

301
00:35:35,016 --> 00:35:38,236
About his brother.

302
00:35:39,649 --> 00:35:43,349
It seems that the mistake
he made curses him.

303
00:35:48,707 --> 00:35:50,517
What are you doing, my Osman?

304
00:35:50,517 --> 00:35:53,017
You should rest!

305
00:35:54,370 --> 00:35:55,710
Oh, Osman!

306
00:36:07,332 --> 00:36:11,162
Osman Bey...
What have I done?

307
00:36:13,452 --> 00:36:15,638
You killed Balgay...

308
00:36:16,522 --> 00:36:22,502
... who tried to make you
kill your brother with spells.

309
00:36:24,602 --> 00:36:31,022
But neither oppression nor tyrants
have come to an end.

310
00:36:32,639 --> 00:36:36,639
We need to stand still.

311
00:36:38,126 --> 00:36:40,286
We need to stay alert.

312
00:36:43,362 --> 00:36:47,362
Stay with me at all times...

313
00:36:48,163 --> 00:36:55,843
... so that we can end
the oppression and the tyrants.

314
00:36:59,400 --> 00:37:00,980
We can end--

315
00:37:01,080 --> 00:37:05,820
My Osman!
My valiant!

316
00:37:06,417 --> 00:37:09,637
My Osman! Hold on!
We'll get to the Tent!

317
00:37:09,997 --> 00:37:10,907
Boran!

318
00:37:15,863 --> 00:37:17,153
Let's go.

319
00:37:26,279 --> 00:37:31,979
I'm here, daughter!
Call me and I'll come flying to you!

320
00:37:33,149 --> 00:37:35,749
The fire inside you will be gone.

321
00:37:36,108 --> 00:37:38,678
The storms in your heart will calm down.

322
00:37:38,837 --> 00:37:42,637
You'll return recovered,
with Allah's help.

323
00:38:06,805 --> 00:38:10,045
It will be over. Don't worry.

324
00:38:16,010 --> 00:38:19,800
Of course it will, my child.
It will be over.

325
00:38:19,800 --> 00:38:26,920
We'll spend beautiful days together once
you recover and come back to the Tent.

326
00:38:37,617 --> 00:38:41,757
Aygül...
My daughter...

327
00:38:42,586 --> 00:38:44,496
My beautiful daughter...

328
00:38:45,469 --> 00:38:52,769
Remember what I've told you. As you have
a father here, you also have a mother.

329
00:38:53,359 --> 00:38:56,439
You're my child too.

330
00:38:57,897 --> 00:39:01,337
You're my life.
You're in my prayers.

331
00:39:01,850 --> 00:39:03,860
May Allah protect you.

332
00:39:42,678 --> 00:39:46,838
It won't take long, my daughter.

333
00:39:48,175 --> 00:39:50,275
I'll visit you.

334
00:39:51,915 --> 00:39:54,985
I'll bring you good news from the Tent.

335
00:39:55,276 --> 00:39:57,006
It won't take long.

336
00:40:10,832 --> 00:40:15,742
My Aygül... This will be
our last separation, hopefully.

337
00:40:17,036 --> 00:40:19,766
Then your father
will always keep you close.

338
00:40:21,319 --> 00:40:22,719
Always.

339
00:40:23,213 --> 00:40:26,033
Come on.
Goodbye, my daughter.

340
00:40:48,553 --> 00:40:49,983
Make it tighter.

341
00:40:54,968 --> 00:40:57,358
- You do the printing.
- Okay.

342
00:41:06,605 --> 00:41:13,265
- May Allah help you!
- Good luck!

343
00:41:24,874 --> 00:41:28,384
May Allah protect you, my daughter.

344
00:41:34,689 --> 00:41:35,799
Aygül!

345
00:41:36,787 --> 00:41:38,197
Where is she going?

346
00:41:41,646 --> 00:41:44,446
Keep working.
I'll be right back.

347
00:41:57,529 --> 00:42:04,029
Dündar Bey! I saw Aygül.
Where is she going?

348
00:42:05,256 --> 00:42:09,256
To find a cure.
It's for good, Hatun, don't worry.

349
00:42:09,725 --> 00:42:13,415
What are you talking about?
Where is my little one's cure?

350
00:42:13,415 --> 00:42:17,285
In Kastamonu. She'll stay
in a dispensary...

351
00:42:17,285 --> 00:42:21,325
... near my brother Yavlak Hasan's
Tent in Seydihan.

352
00:42:22,055 --> 00:42:27,935
There, she'll be protected
and looked after, hopefully.

353
00:42:31,350 --> 00:42:37,330
Hazal... You keep talking about
Yavlak Hasan since you came here.

354
00:42:38,378 --> 00:42:40,668
What are you talking about, Selcan Hatun?

355
00:42:40,949 --> 00:42:46,489
When did she do wrong?
We all owe our lives to her.

356
00:42:47,071 --> 00:42:48,911
Remember, Dündar Bey.

357
00:42:48,991 --> 00:42:53,381
We owe our life to Allah,
and our home to Süleyman Şah!

358
00:42:54,064 --> 00:43:00,464
Why are you sending her to Kastamonu for
a cure? Did Söğüt run out of physicians?

359
00:43:00,767 --> 00:43:02,877
Why are we here for?

360
00:43:04,558 --> 00:43:09,728
You're like a mother.
So I know why you worry, Selcan Hatun.

361
00:43:09,948 --> 00:43:14,168
But change is good.

362
00:43:14,472 --> 00:43:19,582
How can she heal with everything
happening around here?

363
00:43:22,440 --> 00:43:26,900
My heart is already burning.
Please don't push me.

364
00:43:27,956 --> 00:43:32,906
We lost my valiant
Batur because of your thoughtlessness.

365
00:43:33,643 --> 00:43:39,093
Now listen carefully, Dündar.
If something happens to my Aygül...

366
00:43:39,278 --> 00:43:42,998
... then I'll be a burden to you.

367
00:44:01,137 --> 00:44:02,447
Quick!

368
00:44:05,269 --> 00:44:06,629
Clear the way!

369
00:44:07,636 --> 00:44:11,426
- Clear the way!
- Clear the way!

370
00:44:13,282 --> 00:44:14,982
Clear the way!

371
00:44:22,821 --> 00:44:24,911
Clear the way!

372
00:44:27,426 --> 00:44:30,806
Clear!
Clear the way!

373
00:44:56,272 --> 00:44:59,762
Osman!

374
00:45:03,873 --> 00:45:06,913
Is he alive, Bamsı Bey?
Tell me that he's alive!

375
00:45:06,913 --> 00:45:11,763
He's alive. But he's badly hurt!
We need to take care of it!

376
00:45:11,763 --> 00:45:17,643
- Where is Selcan Hatun? Selcan Hatun!
- Osman!

377
00:45:18,025 --> 00:45:21,465
Where is Selcan Hatun?!

378
00:45:21,465 --> 00:45:24,495
- Get out of the way! Osman!
- Selcan Hatun!

379
00:45:24,495 --> 00:45:27,875
- Hold on, Osman!
- My nephew! Osman!

380
00:45:28,067 --> 00:45:31,587
- Osman!
- Say something, Osman!

381
00:45:31,587 --> 00:45:34,527
My Osman! Come on!

382
00:45:39,495 --> 00:45:40,785
Hurry up!

383
00:45:48,651 --> 00:45:53,221
- Osman!
- Hurry up, Boran!

384
00:45:53,674 --> 00:45:54,904
Hurry up!

385
00:46:10,485 --> 00:46:11,465
Brother!

386
00:46:13,162 --> 00:46:16,042
Go in!
Come on, valiants!

387
00:46:17,522 --> 00:46:22,662
My Osman!
Brother!

388
00:46:26,283 --> 00:46:30,983
- Brother!
- My Gündüz! Stop!

389
00:46:30,983 --> 00:46:34,343
Stop! My Gündüz, stop!

390
00:46:34,343 --> 00:46:36,683
We should let Selcan Hatun do her work.

391
00:46:37,006 --> 00:46:41,196
Tell me the truth, Bamsı Bey!
What happened to my brother?

392
00:46:41,389 --> 00:46:45,899
It was Sofia! We made it in time but
he was already wounded.

393
00:46:45,998 --> 00:46:47,618
He was already wounded.

394
00:46:47,618 --> 00:46:49,448
It looks serious, Bamsı Bey!

395
00:46:49,815 --> 00:46:54,915
It is, Dündar Bey. But Selcan Hatun
and Bala will do what's necessary.

396
00:46:54,915 --> 00:46:58,915
We shouldn't disturb them.
Son!

397
00:47:01,686 --> 00:47:07,166
My Allah, take my other arm
but heal my Osman!

398
00:47:10,687 --> 00:47:13,287
Save our Osman, my Allah...

399
00:47:13,952 --> 00:47:15,822
Save our Osman...

400
00:47:30,146 --> 00:47:33,236
Hold on, my Osman.
Hold on.

401
00:47:52,425 --> 00:47:56,115
It's very deep.
What if searing it isn't enough?

402
00:47:56,115 --> 00:47:58,045
What if it doesn't do?

403
00:47:59,324 --> 00:48:02,834
What will we do then, mother?
What will we do without Osman?

404
00:48:03,645 --> 00:48:06,055
Death is the only burden
that doesn't get better.

405
00:48:06,055 --> 00:48:09,575
My Osman is alive. He's breathing.

406
00:48:09,906 --> 00:48:15,256
My valiant will be okay.
He'll be okay.

407
00:48:19,996 --> 00:48:21,476
Hold on, my valiant.

408
00:48:21,822 --> 00:48:24,472
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
[in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate]

409
00:48:25,317 --> 00:48:27,667
With the name of Allah!

410
00:48:31,633 --> 00:48:33,733
With the name of Allah!

411
00:48:36,939 --> 00:48:40,939
Hold on, my Osman.
Stand still!

412
00:48:42,497 --> 00:48:47,897
With the name of Allah!

413
00:49:14,267 --> 00:49:16,103
Damn it!

414
00:49:17,053 --> 00:49:23,083
Send some men to see if Osman returned
to his Tent or died in the forest.

415
00:49:23,379 --> 00:49:28,109
- If he's alive, he'll attack the castle.
- As you order.

416
00:49:28,194 --> 00:49:32,194
Call the knights in. Now!

417
00:49:35,389 --> 00:49:38,889
Alexis!
Come here.

418
00:49:47,751 --> 00:49:51,751
You'll go to our last hope of salvation.

419
00:49:51,924 --> 00:49:57,134
To Aya Nichola. Tell him Sofia asks for
immediate support against the Turks.

420
00:49:57,134 --> 00:49:58,684
As you order!

421
00:49:59,156 --> 00:50:03,686
Aya Nichola? He'll never help us,
Princess. And you know th--

422
00:50:03,686 --> 00:50:04,836
He will!

423
00:50:09,451 --> 00:50:14,491
If this castle falls, the Christian unity
of these lands will fall with it.

424
00:50:17,270 --> 00:50:19,820
Aya Nichola won't refuse this.

425
00:50:58,051 --> 00:50:59,401
He's not okay.

426
00:51:06,653 --> 00:51:08,823
We should be prepared for everything.

427
00:51:14,795 --> 00:51:16,115
My Bey...

428
00:51:27,250 --> 00:51:32,550
Gündüz!
My nephew!

429
00:51:35,660 --> 00:51:37,096
Gündüz Bey!

430
00:51:41,306 --> 00:51:44,996
- Gündüz.
- I can't leave my brother alone.

431
00:51:46,179 --> 00:51:50,519
No. I can't leave my brother alone.

432
00:51:52,679 --> 00:51:56,679
Mother...
What are you saying?

433
00:51:58,914 --> 00:52:01,304
What would a wound do to my brother?

434
00:52:03,775 --> 00:52:06,955
A single wound can't do
anything to my brother.

435
00:52:09,988 --> 00:52:14,418
I can't leave him alone.
I can't. I--

436
00:52:15,595 --> 00:52:17,565
My Gündüz, my child...

437
00:52:18,004 --> 00:52:22,964
My girl Bala is taking care of my Osman.
There's always hope.

438
00:52:23,665 --> 00:52:26,455
There's always hope, child.

439
00:52:29,866 --> 00:52:35,416
I couldn't protect him.
I couldn't protect my brother, Bamsı Bey.

440
00:52:36,482 --> 00:52:38,612
What will I say to my father?

441
00:52:41,092 --> 00:52:44,612
Bamsı Bey?
You know these things.

442
00:52:45,008 --> 00:52:49,008
What will I say to my father if he asks
what happened to Osman?

443
00:52:55,215 --> 00:52:57,495
I couldn't protect him.

444
00:52:59,616 --> 00:53:04,986
Child! My Osman will be okay!
He will be fine.

445
00:53:06,495 --> 00:53:13,475
Don't worry. Calm down.
Stay strong.

446
00:53:14,835 --> 00:53:18,835
Child! You're a Bey!

447
00:53:20,981 --> 00:53:24,981
You must stand still so
the people can too!

448
00:53:25,920 --> 00:53:31,020
You must be strong so we
can be too.

449
00:53:33,174 --> 00:53:34,994
So we can be strong.

450
00:53:43,081 --> 00:53:44,221
Be strong!

451
00:54:44,059 --> 00:54:48,399
What will I say on the doomsday?

452
00:54:50,794 --> 00:54:57,574
I couldn't support him like an uncle
because of my ambition.

453
00:54:58,629 --> 00:55:00,819
I poked my nose into everything he did.

454
00:55:00,819 --> 00:55:06,999
How can I say that I always pushed him
and tried to make him fail?

455
00:55:13,775 --> 00:55:16,575
Don't blame yourself too much, my Dündar.

456
00:55:16,575 --> 00:55:23,385
Don't. You made mistakes.
But everyone makes mistakes.

457
00:55:24,429 --> 00:55:28,039
Isn't regretting the important thing?

458
00:55:28,180 --> 00:55:35,080
Look, you've been on his side for
a long time.

459
00:55:36,182 --> 00:55:45,422
Wouldn't Osman be mad at you if he
got up and heard what you're saying?

460
00:55:45,648 --> 00:55:47,478
Wouldn't he be angry?

461
00:55:47,577 --> 00:55:52,127
Wouldn't he be angry at you
because you were over those things?

462
00:55:56,228 --> 00:55:58,108
What if he can't get up?

463
00:55:59,734 --> 00:56:02,664
What if that valiant passes away?

464
00:56:02,934 --> 00:56:05,634
What will I do then, Hazal?

465
00:56:06,865 --> 00:56:09,105
How will I deal with this remorse?

466
00:56:13,626 --> 00:56:16,276
Pull yourself together, Dündar Bey!

467
00:56:16,408 --> 00:56:20,408
A valiant like Osman won't die so easily.

468
00:56:20,918 --> 00:56:25,368
No. We will pray,
and Allah will heal him.

469
00:56:26,732 --> 00:56:33,302
Don't drop your head. Osman will
get up the same way he always does.

470
00:56:34,994 --> 00:56:39,694
You're like a father to him.
And he's like a son to you

471
00:56:39,862 --> 00:56:47,432
Stand upright. So that he can be motivated
when he gets up and sees you!

472
00:56:49,119 --> 00:56:56,769
You just wait. You'll draw your swords
and go into battles once again.

473
00:56:56,870 --> 00:56:59,690
You'll support each other.

474
00:57:02,546 --> 00:57:03,818
Inshallah.

475
00:57:05,948 --> 00:57:07,559
Inshallah, Hatun.

476
00:57:09,769 --> 00:57:12,932
I just want my Osman to
open his eyes...

477
00:57:14,810 --> 00:57:16,453
...and tell me...

478
00:57:17,551 --> 00:57:19,108
...''Get up, uncle...

479
00:57:19,850 --> 00:57:22,348
...we are going to battle.''...

480
00:57:22,875 --> 00:57:24,820
...and I will march before him.

481
00:57:25,954 --> 00:57:29,669
I will be his shield. As long as...

482
00:57:30,837 --> 00:57:32,877
...my nephew is healthy.

483
00:58:24,827 --> 00:58:26,317
Göktuğ.

484
00:58:54,423 --> 00:58:56,446
Your only legacy for me...

485
00:58:58,014 --> 00:58:59,846
...was your loyalty for Osman Bey.

486
00:59:03,527 --> 00:59:06,062
I came here with this loyalty, brother.

487
00:59:08,326 --> 00:59:09,853
I swear to you...

488
00:59:11,377 --> 00:59:14,359
...from now, we will live in one
body as two souls.

489
00:59:15,655 --> 00:59:17,883
You will be with me...

490
00:59:18,496 --> 00:59:21,294
... every time I swing my sword
against a heathen, brother.

491
00:59:21,593 --> 00:59:23,383
You will be there.

492
00:59:32,329 --> 00:59:37,074
Only the light of death can clean
my sins.

493
00:59:39,616 --> 00:59:41,794
I won't wait long, brother.

494
00:59:42,377 --> 00:59:44,298
I'll join you soon.

495
00:59:46,435 --> 00:59:48,149
My heroic brother.

496
01:00:38,339 --> 01:00:39,669
My Osman.

497
01:00:41,891 --> 01:00:44,979
My valiant. I'm here.
I'm here, husband.

498
01:00:46,619 --> 01:00:50,901
It will be over, Osman.
You will be well again. You'll be well.

499
01:00:53,349 --> 01:00:55,295
Yes, yes, Osman?

500
01:01:03,317 --> 01:01:04,619
Osman?

501
01:01:08,065 --> 01:01:09,077
Osman?

502
01:01:11,832 --> 01:01:16,120
Open your eyes, Osman. Look at me.
Osman?

503
01:01:18,863 --> 01:01:20,833
Look at me. Look at me, Osman.

504
01:01:21,906 --> 01:01:24,675
Open your eyes, my love.
Open it!

505
01:01:24,871 --> 01:01:29,046
Look at me, Osman. Look at me!
Open your eyes! Look at me!

506
01:01:31,251 --> 01:01:35,570
Gündüz Bey, help!
Gündüz Bey, help!

507
01:01:38,399 --> 01:01:39,616
Help!

508
01:01:41,723 --> 01:01:45,826
Osman, look at me, my valiant!
Look at me, my husband.

509
01:01:46,875 --> 01:01:49,973
Osman, open your eyes!
Open your eyes, my love!

510
01:01:50,768 --> 01:01:55,709
Osman! Osman!
Help!

511
01:01:56,384 --> 01:01:59,910
Osman Bey! Osman Bey!
Osman Bey!

512
01:02:01,862 --> 01:02:06,036
What's happening? What is this
rumble? What's happening.

513
01:02:08,911 --> 01:02:13,378
We got news from Osman Bey, my Bey.
We should head there at once.

514
01:02:14,480 --> 01:02:18,237
-Tell me what happened.
-Osman Bey...

515
01:02:20,379 --> 01:02:24,204
What happened to Osman?
Tell me!

516
01:02:25,282 --> 01:02:28,185
He ascended to heaven, my Beg.
My condolences.

517
01:02:35,452 --> 01:02:37,163
Son...

518
01:02:38,577 --> 01:02:41,178
What are you saying, son?

519
01:02:43,099 --> 01:02:46,473
What are you saying, son?
What are you saying?

520
01:02:49,147 --> 01:02:50,035
My Bey.

521
01:02:53,975 --> 01:02:58,364
Osman, Osman!
Osman!

522
01:03:02,358 --> 01:03:07,868
My nephew! It's because of me...

523
01:03:09,141 --> 01:03:14,920
It's because of me!
I couldn't stand behind him...

524
01:03:16,989 --> 01:03:20,264
Dündar Bey, don't let yourself go.

525
01:03:21,146 --> 01:03:24,429
It's because of me, it's my fault.
I couldn't stand behind him.

526
01:03:25,658 --> 01:03:28,510
I couldn't stand behind my nephew.

527
01:03:28,924 --> 01:03:32,342
Oh, my Osman.
It's my fault!

528
01:03:35,673 --> 01:03:36,844
Osman!

529
01:03:38,109 --> 01:03:40,731
My nephew!
Osman!

530
01:04:26,406 --> 01:04:27,394
Son...

531
01:04:30,462 --> 01:04:32,694
Is it true, son?

532
01:04:41,373 --> 01:04:42,830
Gündüz Bey.

533
01:04:44,443 --> 01:04:47,063
People are waiting for
explanation.

534
01:05:17,727 --> 01:05:23,630
My brother, Osman...
...is a mortal like every one of us.

535
01:05:30,453 --> 01:05:32,803
And the end of every mortal is...

536
01:05:39,972 --> 01:05:42,353
...leaving this world.

537
01:05:52,407 --> 01:05:55,503
What is deathless is Allah.

538
01:06:03,017 --> 01:06:07,535
Humans are mortal...

539
01:06:09,497 --> 01:06:12,011
...and destined to vanish.

540
01:06:15,432 --> 01:06:18,241
And time belongs to...

541
01:06:19,663 --> 01:06:21,818
...Allah only.

542
01:06:22,653 --> 01:06:24,793
Oh, Osman...

543
01:06:26,091 --> 01:06:28,099
Oh, my nephew...

544
01:06:30,179 --> 01:06:33,075
What will last forever is...

545
01:06:33,765 --> 01:06:36,027
...the cause of Allah.

546
01:06:38,326 --> 01:06:41,348
O valiant people of Kayıs!

547
01:06:44,944 --> 01:06:46,693
Osmans,...

548
01:06:48,138 --> 01:06:49,298
...Gündüzs,...

549
01:06:50,108 --> 01:06:51,664
...Abdurrahman Ghazis...

550
01:06:53,276 --> 01:06:55,699
...Borans and Ayazs...

551
01:06:59,121 --> 01:07:00,799
...Bamsıs...

552
01:07:01,751 --> 01:07:03,559
...are temporary.

553
01:07:14,363 --> 01:07:16,823
What is constant is...

554
01:07:20,684 --> 01:07:22,760
...the love of holy war...

555
01:07:24,055 --> 01:07:26,284
...in our hearts.

556
01:07:26,811 --> 01:07:49,975
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!

557
01:08:22,872 --> 01:08:24,904
I've brought you an evangel,
princess.

558
01:08:25,773 --> 01:08:26,653
Speak.

559
01:08:28,276 --> 01:08:30,034
Osman Bey has died, your majesty.

560
01:08:43,181 --> 01:08:44,960
Finally...

561
01:08:48,364 --> 01:08:50,600
Jesus Christ, thank god.

562
01:08:56,093 --> 01:08:59,340
We got rid of that wretched man
named Osman!

563
01:09:00,610 --> 01:09:02,291
Hear it out!

564
01:09:02,291 --> 01:09:07,661
Prepare the tables! Send the word
to every corner of the castle.

565
01:09:10,213 --> 01:09:14,165
Osman kicked the bucket!
Now it's time for a feast!

566
01:09:27,836 --> 01:09:30,270
Finally, it is over.

567
01:09:34,298 --> 01:09:36,580
I avenged you, father.

568
01:09:41,644 --> 01:09:43,899
Now you can rest in peace.

569
01:09:56,977 --> 01:09:58,994
Thank god.

570
01:10:56,968 --> 01:10:58,775
Forgive me, my Allah.

571
01:11:09,348 --> 01:11:12,072
Aygül... Where is Aygül?

572
01:11:12,924 --> 01:11:14,436
She was here, Saltukhan.

573
01:11:35,478 --> 01:11:37,441
What are you looking at, fool?
Come on!

574
01:11:42,491 --> 01:11:45,850
This lunatic will be trouble.
God damn it.

575
01:13:50,149 --> 01:13:55,734
My dear father, the great man who
made me who I am...

576
01:13:56,316 --> 01:13:59,269
For Yannis' brave soul!

577
01:15:28,506 --> 01:15:31,514
Knights of Aya Nichola are coming.
Inform the princess.

578
01:16:15,960 --> 01:16:18,606
The aid we were waiting from Aya Nichola
is here.

579
01:16:29,492 --> 01:16:35,539
Aya Nichola, Lord of Inegol, sent his
brave men to our aid.

580
01:16:48,570 --> 01:16:50,518
I raise my glass...

581
01:16:51,547 --> 01:16:54,593
...for Osman's burning soul in hell!

582
01:19:06,220 --> 01:19:09,336
Brave knights of Aya Nichola!

583
01:19:10,158 --> 01:19:12,593
Welcome to our castle!

584
01:19:28,097 --> 01:19:31,936
I see that Aya Nichola is as kind...

585
01:19:32,560 --> 01:19:35,200
...as he is brave.

586
01:19:35,452 --> 01:19:41,392
I'm sure that a chivalrous
lord such as Aya Nichola...

587
01:19:42,738 --> 01:19:47,132
...sent a beautiful carpet
for our feet.

588
01:20:20,939 --> 01:20:23,070
Who did this?

589
01:20:25,563 --> 01:20:27,719
Who did this?

590
01:20:56,048 --> 01:20:58,694
Osman son of Ertugrul Ghazi!

591
01:21:08,918 --> 01:21:10,182
Osman...

592
01:21:27,582 --> 01:21:30,586
My wolf-eyed brother, don't
let yourself down.

593
01:21:30,586 --> 01:21:33,066
It's not the time to say goodbye.

594
01:21:37,337 --> 01:21:38,485
Osman!

595
01:21:39,158 --> 01:21:42,045
It's not the time I say goodbye.

596
01:21:43,627 --> 01:21:48,131
Now it's time for conquest.

597
01:21:54,678 --> 01:21:58,756
No one else other than Sheikh Edebali
and...

598
01:22:00,722 --> 01:22:03,300
...my faithful friends...

599
01:22:06,211 --> 01:22:11,606
...will know about our play.

600
01:22:16,122 --> 01:22:18,620
Let them think...

601
01:22:20,442 --> 01:22:22,914
...I am dead.

602
01:22:23,161 --> 01:22:26,632
I've brought death upon your door, Sofia.

603
01:22:35,061 --> 01:22:38,171
Soldiers, ambush!

604
01:22:38,565 --> 01:22:40,679
Charge!

605
01:27:40,108 --> 01:27:42,895
-Sofia!
-Stop him!

606
01:27:47,302 --> 01:27:48,918
Stop him!

607
01:28:18,381 --> 01:28:23,434
Wherever you run into, Sofia,
you can't outrun your death.

608
01:29:11,885 --> 01:29:16,258
Now I will finish what I left
unfinished.

609
01:29:19,514 --> 01:29:22,060
Come, then, Osman.

610
01:29:23,689 --> 01:29:26,435
This castle will be your graveyard.

611
01:30:46,062 --> 01:30:49,115
Attack, valiants!
Attack!

612
01:30:50,441 --> 01:30:54,052
Ya Allah! With the name of Allah!

613
01:31:05,414 --> 01:31:08,580
Fight, valiants!
Fight, dervishes!

614
01:32:10,832 --> 01:32:13,235
-Come on!
-Come on, Gündüz!

615
01:33:09,995 --> 01:33:12,616
Come on, warriors, come on!

616
01:33:47,759 --> 01:33:53,702
Sofia! You have nowhere else
to go.

617
01:34:00,990 --> 01:34:05,973
Every time I see this little wound,
I will remember you.

618
01:34:08,187 --> 01:34:10,921
You won't be remembered by anyone.

619
01:34:13,127 --> 01:34:15,527
I will banish you and your kind...

620
01:34:15,527 --> 01:34:19,053
...to the damned steppes where
you came.

621
01:34:30,219 --> 01:34:33,782
We came to clean these lands...

622
01:34:34,623 --> 01:34:37,527
...which you polluted with
blasphemy.

623
01:34:39,543 --> 01:34:43,876
Whatever you do...

624
01:34:44,484 --> 01:34:47,079
...these lands will belong to Muslims.

625
01:34:49,998 --> 01:34:54,300
Now it's time your time to answer
for your crimes.

626
01:34:57,455 --> 01:35:00,673
That won't be as easy as you think, Osman.

627
01:35:22,498 --> 01:35:26,928
Your evilness will have no profit for you,
Sofia.

628
01:35:27,586 --> 01:35:30,566
The curse of god!

629
01:35:31,619 --> 01:35:34,879
Damn Turk!

630
01:35:35,278 --> 01:35:39,528
We Turks are the heat of Allah
against the cruels!

631
01:36:14,658 --> 01:36:17,528
Sofia!

632
01:36:27,610 --> 01:36:31,010
Stop Osman!
Sofia!

633
01:36:39,070 --> 01:36:46,220
Princess.
Princess!

634
01:36:50,130 --> 01:36:53,000
I won't give them even your body.

635
01:36:54,191 --> 01:36:58,981
I will not!

636
01:36:59,321 --> 01:37:01,931
Get her up!

637
01:37:30,012 --> 01:37:32,612
Ya Allah!
Ya Fettah (one of Allah's qualities.)

638
01:37:38,432 --> 01:37:41,092
Ya Allah!
Ya Fettah (one of Allah's qualities.)

639
01:37:44,650 --> 01:37:48,660
Attack, my valiants, attack!

640
01:39:55,691 --> 01:39:58,691
Brothers.

641
01:40:04,639 --> 01:40:07,109
Brother.

642
01:40:36,382 --> 01:40:43,452
Thank Allah who granted us...

643
01:40:44,189 --> 01:40:47,512
...with this conquer.

644
01:40:47,512 --> 01:40:50,802
Thank Allah.

645
01:40:50,918 --> 01:40:57,428
From now on, Kulucahisar Castle is
muslim place.

646
01:41:01,933 --> 01:41:21,533
Allah-u Akbar!
(Allah is the greatest!)

647
01:41:21,716 --> 01:41:25,246
Inform the tent immediately.

648
01:41:25,275 --> 01:41:33,325
Today, we conquer!
Today, Kayıs' feast day!

649
01:41:37,759 --> 01:41:44,889
My relatives, my uncle, my friends...

650
01:41:45,252 --> 01:41:49,672
- let them all come.
- Command is yours, my Bey

651
01:41:50,111 --> 01:41:53,111
Mashaallah (praise be),
my valiant.

652
01:42:50,107 --> 01:42:52,427
Don't be afraid.

653
01:42:54,498 --> 01:42:57,478
Don't wince.

654
01:43:14,999 --> 01:43:19,429
For the sake of Allah, who is the
creator of earth.

655
01:43:21,292 --> 01:43:27,342
For the sake of our prophet
Muhammed Mustafa.

656
01:43:28,170 --> 01:43:31,690
For the sake of his generation.

657
01:43:31,959 --> 01:43:36,665
For the sake of one hundred and twenty
four thousand prophets.

658
01:43:36,805 --> 01:43:38,895
I...

659
01:43:42,019 --> 01:43:46,169
swear on my weapon...

660
01:43:46,937 --> 01:43:54,287
Your goods, your life, your fatih,
your honor...

661
01:43:54,734 --> 01:43:58,064
all are entrusted to us.

662
01:44:17,955 --> 01:44:20,645
Come here.

663
01:44:45,745 --> 01:44:48,715
Come.

664
01:45:13,837 --> 01:45:19,657
The cruels saw Turks' heat.

665
01:45:20,892 --> 01:45:28,862
Now, the opresseds shall see
our compassion.

666
01:45:39,831 --> 01:45:45,131
Boran, reimburse these people.

667
01:45:45,403 --> 01:45:47,683
Command is yours, my Bey.

668
01:46:20,699 --> 01:46:23,379
Brothers!

669
01:46:25,313 --> 01:46:28,473
- Bamsı Bey.
- Hey, my valiant!

670
01:46:28,479 --> 01:46:31,249
Ey Masha Allah(praise be)

671
01:46:33,396 --> 01:46:38,036
Masha Allah (praise be!) my valiant!
Well done!

672
01:46:41,620 --> 01:46:45,740
Brother, brother.

673
01:47:20,422 --> 01:47:23,292
Your pain is huge, my Bey.

674
01:47:23,661 --> 01:47:27,441
You loved Osman as your son.

675
01:47:27,523 --> 01:47:31,703
I lost another son of mine, Hatun.

676
01:47:33,539 --> 01:47:39,509
Now, when I look back, I see that...

677
01:47:40,319 --> 01:47:45,239
All of it is my fault.

678
01:47:46,228 --> 01:47:51,258
Don't, Dündar Bey, it's not your fault.

679
01:47:51,270 --> 01:47:56,528
Osman impressed us by his bravery.
He fought for his tent.

680
01:47:56,528 --> 01:48:02,088
He became a martyr for the love of Allah.
It's not your fault. Don't act like that.

681
01:48:11,489 --> 01:48:13,519
Son.

682
01:48:16,743 --> 01:48:21,523
Your face is like a wet weekend.
What happened?

683
01:48:22,769 --> 01:48:26,179
- Osman
- Yeah?

684
01:48:26,179 --> 01:48:29,239
He didn't die.

685
01:48:31,535 --> 01:48:36,475
He tricked us and Sofia to conquer the
castle, mother.

686
01:48:46,603 --> 01:48:51,623
Do you hear what you are saying, son?

687
01:48:53,116 --> 01:49:00,376
While we are weeping on his grave, he and
Gündüz, Bamsı Bey went to the castle.

688
01:49:00,485 --> 01:49:04,235
They conquered the castle with their Alps.

689
01:49:06,344 --> 01:49:13,314
This is such a time that we witness every
shape of evilness, Dündar Bey!

690
01:49:13,438 --> 01:49:17,998
Here is the betrayal of your son who you
were weeping for.

691
01:49:18,275 --> 01:49:22,225
He even avoids the castle from you.

692
01:49:29,101 --> 01:49:33,851
Look what is your value in his eyes!

693
01:49:36,128 --> 01:49:41,748
There's more, father.
Osman invites you to the castle.

694
01:49:49,642 --> 01:49:54,152
He wants you to witness his victory.

695
01:50:00,774 --> 01:50:02,464
An invitation...

696
01:50:06,692 --> 01:50:10,002
needs to be accepted.

697
01:50:12,046 --> 01:50:14,046
Yeah.

698
01:50:25,338 --> 01:50:27,251
Go.

699
01:50:27,251 --> 01:50:30,041
Don't let your father be alone, son.

700
01:50:31,296 --> 01:50:33,456
Son.

701
01:50:34,012 --> 01:50:37,809
Comprehend what betrayal is.

702
01:50:37,809 --> 01:50:44,659
So that you don't end up like...

703
01:50:44,965 --> 01:50:48,435
Batur, who was killed by Osman.

704
01:51:44,651 --> 01:51:48,074
Those are non-muslims died in the war.

705
01:51:48,074 --> 01:51:54,204
But you look at them pityingly.
What's the meaning of this, my Sheik?

706
01:51:54,327 --> 01:51:59,527
You see them as dead non muslims.

707
01:52:00,809 --> 01:52:06,589
When I look at them, I see unlucky people
that we couldn't teach.

708
01:52:58,966 --> 01:53:06,416
Conquer is the first step of the
plane tree you saw in your dream, son.

709
01:53:06,851 --> 01:53:16,381
Inshaallah, you will be the voice of
the oppressed.

710
01:53:16,514 --> 01:53:20,184
Inshaallah, my Sheik, inshaallah.

711
01:53:20,308 --> 01:53:24,808
- Our conquer shall be mubarak, Bey.
- Eyvallah Hatun (thank you)

712
01:53:34,793 --> 01:53:38,952
He is İsa Sofu from our Yarens.

713
01:53:38,952 --> 01:53:42,682
He came from Samarkand.

714
01:53:57,218 --> 01:54:03,298
My relatives sent this Kayı
flag for you, Osman Bey.

715
01:54:13,434 --> 01:54:16,584
This holy conquest is a fate.

716
01:54:32,365 --> 01:54:34,935
Thanks to the valiants who are
of Yesevi descent...

717
01:54:35,482 --> 01:54:38,072
and build prayer bridges between...

718
01:54:38,172 --> 01:54:41,132
Söğüt and Samarkand.

719
01:54:43,365 --> 01:54:48,185
Inshaallah, this flag...

720
01:54:48,688 --> 01:54:51,688
will be flown
in more castles...

721
01:54:51,807 --> 01:54:57,237
with the Ghazis, son.

722
01:54:58,176 --> 01:55:01,886
Now, fly this flag...

723
01:55:02,483 --> 01:55:05,403
in the castle you won with your weapons.

724
01:56:08,955 --> 01:56:11,985
I think you've heard my Osman's victory?

725
01:56:13,011 --> 01:56:15,961
That's why your eyes twinkle.

726
01:56:17,987 --> 01:56:21,547
Did you know about Osman's game?

727
01:56:26,987 --> 01:56:29,767
Why did you hide it from us?

728
01:56:31,074 --> 01:56:35,074
-Do you know how to keep a secret?
-Yes, of course.

729
01:56:35,924 --> 01:56:37,014
Come here.

730
01:56:40,930 --> 01:56:42,980
My Osman knows it well.

731
01:56:43,268 --> 01:56:47,268
Even his beard doesn't know
what he thinks.

732
01:56:49,000 --> 01:56:53,000
Now, if you'll excuse me... We have a
victory feast tonight.

733
01:56:54,854 --> 01:56:57,044
We have to prepare for it.

734
01:57:18,128 --> 01:57:19,168
Is it done?

735
01:57:26,279 --> 01:57:29,109
Is the duty done?

736
01:57:29,804 --> 01:57:30,844
No.

737
01:57:33,030 --> 01:57:34,940
She ran away.

738
01:57:36,247 --> 01:57:39,667
What do you mean that Aygül ran away?

739
01:57:40,212 --> 01:57:41,942
We looked everywhere.

740
01:57:42,462 --> 01:57:44,162
But we couldn't find her.

741
01:57:45,593 --> 01:57:47,093
We don't know where she is.

742
01:57:55,554 --> 01:57:57,124
Hazal Hatun.

743
01:57:57,664 --> 01:57:59,614
Why is Saltuk brother here?

744
01:58:02,410 --> 01:58:04,450
Where is Aygül?

745
01:58:06,646 --> 01:58:08,296
Mad girl.

746
01:58:12,365 --> 01:58:14,405
She ran away.

747
01:59:20,973 --> 01:59:22,413
You don't forgive...

748
01:59:23,230 --> 01:59:25,440
betrayals, right?

749
01:59:43,927 --> 01:59:45,737
You'll pay for..

750
01:59:46,388 --> 01:59:48,478
what you did.

751
01:59:48,712 --> 01:59:50,532
There's no excuse and compensation...

752
01:59:51,631 --> 01:59:53,801
for betrayal.

753
02:00:05,153 --> 02:00:09,043
He never had a suspicion
about me killing his son...

754
02:00:09,671 --> 02:00:13,671
- and giving me his daughter.
- What did I do, Osman?

755
02:00:14,284 --> 02:00:15,774
What did I do?

756
02:00:16,546 --> 02:00:18,916
Forgiving cruels...

757
02:00:19,270 --> 02:00:21,830
is a darkness for the innocent.

758
02:00:23,216 --> 02:00:27,216
It's not right in our religion!

759
02:00:30,023 --> 02:00:32,333
Betrayals are done, uncle.

760
02:00:33,744 --> 02:00:35,484
Today is the day of victory.

761
02:00:37,330 --> 02:00:38,490
Today...

762
